<title>USA: U.S. offshore oil services sector sharply down.</title>
<headline>U.S. offshore oil services sector sharply down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reports of downgrades for the oilfield services sector and weakness after an announcement on Friday that privately-owned Edison Chouest had placed an order for 10 offshore oilfield support vessels hit the sector hard on Monday.</p>
<p>In late trade on Monday, shares in Hvide Marine had plummeted 5-3/8, or 25 percent to 15-7/8.</p>
<p>&quot;What happened is that Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette downgraded the sector and that combined with the Edison news hurt the stock,&quot; said a spokeswoman for the company.</p>
<p>No one at DLJ was immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
